{"content":[{"c":["ADASA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Town mentioned only in the period of the Maccabean revolt. Judas Maccabeus defeated the Syrian army under Nicanor in 161 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," at Adasa. The victory was celebrated annually on the 13th of Adar (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.7.40,45,49","r":"1Macc.7.40,45,49","rawR":"1Macc.7.40,45,49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.7.40,45,49","value":"1Macc.7.40,45,49"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Macc 7:40, 45, 49"},"). The modern site is probably Khirbet ’Adassa, 7 miles (11 kilometers) from Beth-horon."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Leader of a group of Babylonian exiles returning to Judah who were unable to prove their Jewish ancestry (",{"href":"?bref=1Esd.5.36","r":"1Esd.5.36","rawR":"1Esd.5.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Esd.5.36","value":"1Esd.5.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Esd 5:36"},"). The same name, spelled Addon, seems to refer to an otherwise unidentified place in the Babylonian Empire (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.61","r":"Neh.7.61","rawR":"Neh.7.61","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.61","value":"Neh.7.61"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:61"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Adasa","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Macc 7:40, 45, 49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.7.40,45,49","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.7.40,45,49","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.7.40,45,49"},{"anchorText":"1 Esd 5:36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Esd.5.36","rawQueryValue":"1Esd.5.36","sourceRefExact":"1Esd.5.36"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:61","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.7.61","rawQueryValue":"Neh.7.61","sourceRefExact":"Neh.7.61"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d7e0ac644974d1046d21921ac471dab8fcba9fc437537cad3f46a3569289ac15","sourceItemName":"Adasa","sourceItemOrder":108,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Adasa","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Adasa","title":"Adasa","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}